          "type": "text",
          "x": 100,
          "y": 760,
          "width": 470,
          "height": 480,
          "text": "At midnight, when the polar sun skims low along the northern horizon, the silence is broken only by the seismic thunder of calving seracs collapsing into the sea.\n\nThese ancient glacial tongues, compressed over millennia of snowfall, release miniature tsunamis across the fjord, rocking our scientific vessel and scattering fulmars across the mist.",
